fix: background config rejected by schemastery (plugin failed to load)

The ackground sub-config was declared as a volatile object with volatile
fields, which schemastery rejects: "volatile fields require a fixed object
path without an enclosing volatile field". The Config constructor threw at
load time, so the whole plugin failed to apply in the host — every route
(including /state) returned 404 and no shell-switch tool mounted.

Drop .volatile() at every level of ackground: these are static config
values with schema defaults, not per-read runtime cells. Config now builds.
